// Single-worker schedule for 20-index-cast-permute (TASK-0431 AC#2).
//
// One worker (`host`): the identity permutation `out[idx(i)] <-- pass(in[i])`
// needs the whole of `out` mutable on one worker, trivially satisfied (no
// transfers, no cross-worker fan-in). The pure index kernel `idx` and the
// pure passthrough `pass` are placed on the same worker — `idx` is called
// inline at the scatter index site with a BARE ITER VAR argument, which is
// the X1' cast shape this example exists to exercise (TASK-0431).
//
// DELIBERATELY single-worker only. A distributed variant would partition
// the `i` loop, but the cast shape under test (`kernels::idx((i) as i32)`)
// is identical in single- and multi-worker codegen (the index expression
// is rendered by the shared `render_int_expr`), so the single-worker cell
// is the minimal sufficient build-clean witness. Adding a distributed
// variant would broaden coverage but is out of AC#2 scope.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host };

    place load_input  on host;
    place save_output on host;
    place idx         on host;
    place pass        on host;

    // No loop transforms, no transfer directives (single worker).
}
